    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test passing).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `membershipNumber` is a pure derivation of two fields the owner already carries (`customerCode` + `registrationDate`), exactly like the existing `householdId`/`displayName` derived response fields. So I added it as a read-only response projection rather than a stored column or a new pipeline step.\n\nTwo files touched, each edit small and low-context:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared a new read-only `membershipNumber` string property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"membershipNumber\", expression = \"java(owner.getCustomerCode() + \\\"-M\\\" + String.format(\\\"%02d\\\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100))\")\n   ```\n   `getYear() % 100` with `%02d` yields the two-digit year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`). `registrationDate` is guaranteed non-null by the time the response is built (`BuildOwner` defaults it to today).\n\n## Why this keeps structural impact low\n\nI put the logic on `OwnerMapper` (a small interface, low `WMC_other`) instead of adding a getter to the large `Owner` entity or a new function class + YAML wiring + DB column. The single changed method (`toOwnerDto`) has CC 1 and one added line, and no existing method grew. No new stored state, no pipeline change, no `Owner.java` edit.",
